23. **End-of-Run "Impact Report" Share Card** — auto-generated shareable card summarizing stats in real-world terms (ties to 3.14) — marketing/demo gold.
24. **Accessible Colorblind-Safe Family Iconography** — small icon badges (not just color) above enemies for family identification — accessibility AND judge-friendly polish signal.
25. **"Roots Below" Secondary Layer** — a subtle parallax underground layer showing root health as a second, purely visual health indicator — reinforces "what you don't see matters too."
26. **Dynamic Difficulty Titles** — instead of "Wave 45," show flavor labels like "The Smog Thickens" or "The Rivers Run Clear" reflecting current PI/vitality state — replaces sterile numbers with narrative texture.
27. **Achievement-Driven Ecopedia Bonus Facts** — completing mastery challenges (3.10) unlocks *bonus* deeper facts beyond the standard entry, rewarding engaged players with more content.
28. **"Plant a Real Tree" Partnership Hook** *(post-launch, optional)* — placeholder hook in credits/menu for a potential real-world tree-planting partnership — huge extra credit for an environmental-fair jury, even just as a stated future intent.
29. **Low-Spec "Calm Mode" Toggle** — reduces particle density/screen shake for accessibility and also doubles as a slower-paced "just relax and defend" mode — broadens audience.
30. **Meta "Ecosystem Journal" Auto-Summary** — after every session, one auto-written sentence log ("Day 14: You survived 12 minutes, cleared 340 pollutants, but a Heatwave hurt the canopy.") stored in a scrollable journal — turns pure stats into a lightweight ongoing narrative without any dialogue writing needed.

